# Zig Style

Do not restate `zig-nesting.mdc`, `zig-testing.mdc`, or `zig-arraylist-api.mdc`.

## Naming

- No redundant names in fully-qualified namespaces: `list.append`, not `list.appendToList`
- `callconv(.c)` for C callbacks (Wayland, libdrm event handlers)
- Prefer typed pointers over `*anyopaque` when the type is known

## Allocators

- Name by lifetime: `gpa` (general-purpose heap) vs `arena` (scoped bump)
- Never `std.heap.page_allocator` in tests — see `zig-testing.mdc`

```zig
// ❌ BAD
const allocator = std.heap.page_allocator;

// ✅ GOOD
const gpa = testing.allocator;
var arena = std.heap.ArenaAllocator.init(gpa);
defer arena.deinit();
```

## Assertions

- `std.debug.assert` is for invariants; recoverable failures return errors
- Pair asserts: **before write** (precondition) and **after read** (observed value)
- Doc comments: **assume** = unchecked illegal behavior; **assert** = safety-checked
- `unreachable` only when proven

```zig
// before write
std.debug.assert(!self.waiting_flip);
self.front = back;

// after read
std.debug.assert(user_data != null);
```
